1
00:01:13,507 --> 00:01:15,307
I don't care how
much they offered you.

2
00:01:15,442 --> 00:01:17,934
We're not selling till
the season's over, okay?

3
00:01:18,111 --> 00:01:19,943
Twenty grand, Keith.

4
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:22,048
Twenty grand for
an unproven colt.

5
00:01:22,215 --> 00:01:25,242
Look, he's
Mr. Moonshine's full brother.

6
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,717
If Mr. Moonshine keeps winning,

7
00:01:26,887 --> 00:01:30,790
that yearling out there's gonna
be worth 40 grand, trust me.

8
00:01:30,958 --> 00:01:34,190
I know you like to bet, but
what if he doesn't keep winning?

9
00:01:34,962 --> 00:01:36,988
I don't have the stomach
for gambling that you do.

10
00:01:37,164 --> 00:01:41,534
That's what makes us a good
team. Your brains, my guts.

11
00:01:45,405 --> 00:01:49,172
So, uh, what happened
to Royal T last week?

12
00:01:49,343 --> 00:01:54,179
- She didn't even place.
- The other jockey boxed her in.

13
00:01:54,348 --> 00:01:55,976
Don't worry, it
won't happen again.

14
00:01:56,984 --> 00:01:58,714
I fired him.

15
00:01:58,952 --> 00:01:59,976
See you.

16
00:02:46,867 --> 00:02:49,427
Hey, old Whiz Kid here looked
pretty good today, don't you think?

17
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:50,593
Yeah, looked great.

18
00:02:50,771 --> 00:02:52,706
Yeah, think it's time we
got him to Redway Downs,

19
00:02:52,873 --> 00:02:55,069
got him some real track work.

20
00:02:55,242 --> 00:02:57,442
Whatever you say. That's
why we're paying you big bucks.

21
00:02:57,611 --> 00:02:59,239
Janice back yet?

22
00:02:59,413 --> 00:03:01,575
Coming in right now.

23
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:09,146
Hi.

24
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:13,792
I had a great ride. You
should have come with me.

25
00:03:16,897 --> 00:03:18,593
Where's Keith?

26
00:03:19,299 --> 00:03:22,861
- Didn't you ask him for dinner?
- He had plans.

27
00:03:23,937 --> 00:03:26,930
- What's wrong?
- We got another letter.

28
00:03:28,709 --> 00:03:30,871
So who am I supposed
to be sleeping with now?

29
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,376
It doesn't say.

30
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:33,673
So, what else is new?

31
00:03:33,847 --> 00:03:37,716
This one says you were with someone
the night I was in Savannah last week.

32
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:40,046
- And you believe it?
- I tried to call you that night

33
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,244
but you weren't home.

34
00:03:41,421 --> 00:03:45,119
I told you already, I went to dinner
and a movie with Melissa that night.

35
00:03:45,292 --> 00:03:47,492
Then you went for a drive,
didn't get home till after 1.

36
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:50,895
- What am I supposed to believe?
- I don't give a damn what you believe.

37
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:53,124
They don't mean anything?
Who's sending these?

38
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:54,324
Why would they send them?

39
00:03:54,501 --> 00:03:56,061
I don't know who's sending them.

40
00:03:57,404 --> 00:04:01,603
Janice, I love you, but you
are making it very difficult.

41
00:04:01,775 --> 00:04:05,234
I'm really hurt that you
believe some crackpot,

42
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:08,473
who won't even sign his
name, instead of your own wife.

43
00:04:08,648 --> 00:04:10,768
I tried to call yesterday
and you weren't home either.

44
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:12,283
Stop it, Mike.

45
00:04:12,452 --> 00:04:17,083
This jealously thing has gotta
stop. It's gonna destroy us.

46
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,249
Just tell me where you were.

47
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:24,764
I was out buying your stupid
birthday present, that's where I was.

48
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,563
Janice, I'm sorry.

49
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:31,435
Oh, just leave me alone.

50
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,557
Mr. Matlock.

51
00:04:56,997 --> 00:04:58,727
Hi.

52
00:04:58,899 --> 00:05:02,995
I'm Mike Wilson and I
need your help. Can we talk?

53
00:05:04,571 --> 00:05:07,837
- You mean now? In here?
- It's kind of urgent.

54
00:05:08,008 --> 00:05:10,204
Well, I have to get
back to a hearing.

55
00:05:10,377 --> 00:05:13,176
Uh, call me at my office.
I'm listed in Willis Spring.

56
00:05:13,346 --> 00:05:15,440
I've been working
out of my house lately,

57
00:05:15,615 --> 00:05:17,914
kind of cut down
on the overhead.

58
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:20,815
So you just call me
anytime you, uh...

59
00:05:31,698 --> 00:05:33,724
Uh, Mr. Wilson?

60
00:05:36,603 --> 00:05:38,299
Mr. Wilson?

61
00:06:12,439 --> 00:06:13,566
Hi.

62
00:06:16,409 --> 00:06:17,638
How did you get in here?

63
00:06:17,811 --> 00:06:19,837
I know I'm imposing
and I'm sorry.

64
00:06:20,013 --> 00:06:22,312
But like I said before,
this is important.

65
00:06:22,482 --> 00:06:25,213
- How did you get in here?
- The door.

66
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,513
Well, you just go
back out the door.

67
00:06:27,687 --> 00:06:29,349
Listen to me, okay?

68
00:06:30,156 --> 00:06:33,126
You don't understand. You're
the only one who can help me.

69
00:06:33,293 --> 00:06:35,319
- Out.
- My wife is on trial for murder,

70
00:06:35,495 --> 00:06:37,487
only the lawyer she's
got is incompetent.

71
00:06:37,664 --> 00:06:39,963
Well, not incompetent
really, just unqualified.

72
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:43,160
- See, he's an old family friend.
- Out!

73
00:06:44,304 --> 00:06:46,569
You couldn't have come
in this door, it's bolted.

74
00:06:48,141 --> 00:06:49,336
Maybe the other door.

75
00:06:49,743 --> 00:06:51,234
You gotta talk to
him, advise him,

76
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:53,277
maybe even take
over the case for him.

77
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:54,846
The back door's locked too.

78
00:06:55,015 --> 00:06:56,483
Please, you've gotta help me.

79
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:59,848
Scott Ainsley, that's her
lawyer. Do you know him?

80
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,044
I know of him.

81
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:04,113
Talk to him about Janice's
case tomorrow morning.

82
00:07:04,291 --> 00:07:07,887
- Talk to him about what?
- His strategy. How he's pleading her.

83
00:07:08,061 --> 00:07:09,529
It's not my place.

84
00:07:09,696 --> 00:07:13,827
I love my wife more than anything,
and her future is at stake here.

85
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,128
And I am gonna do
whatever I have to to help her.

86
00:07:16,303 --> 00:07:20,172
Please, talk to Scott
Ainsley first thing tomorrow.

87
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,467
Out!

88
00:07:25,078 --> 00:07:26,478
Please.

89
00:07:44,264 --> 00:07:46,290
Mr. Ainsley?

90
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,729
Hi, Ben Matlock.

91
00:07:47,901 --> 00:07:50,894
We met at a Georgia State Bar
meeting a couple of years back.

92
00:07:51,071 --> 00:07:53,802
- Right. It's good to see you again.
- Good to see you.

93
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:57,706
Could I just speak with
you in private, please?

94
00:07:58,445 --> 00:08:02,644
Yes, of course. Um, go on over
to my office. I'll be right there.

95
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,851
- Is that Ms. Wilson?
- Yes.

96
00:08:08,021 --> 00:08:12,857
Well, uh, I don't know whether
her husband said anything to you,

97
00:08:13,226 --> 00:08:16,822
but, uh, he seems to feel
that you might not be...

98
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:19,557
- Her husband? Mike?
- Yeah.

99
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:23,170
He came over to my house last
night and he expressed some concern...

100
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,861
He came over to your house?

101
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:29,305
- Yeah. Yeah. And he said that he...
- Is this some kind of sick joke?

102
00:08:31,111 --> 00:08:33,410
- How's that?
- Mike Wilson is dead.

103
00:08:34,314 --> 00:08:36,806
My client, although she was
temporarily insane at the time,

104
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:38,110
killed him.

105
00:08:39,252 --> 00:08:42,279
- Say again?
- Mike Wilson is dead.

106
00:08:43,223 --> 00:08:44,350
Mike Wilson's dead?

107
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,391
I have things to
do, Mr. Matlock.

108
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,859
And I should think a man
of your stature does too.

109
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:53,728
So if there's some kind of punch
line here, could we get to it, please.

110
00:08:55,068 --> 00:08:58,630
Oh, no, there's no punch line.

111
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:03,006
Mike Wilson's dead.

112
00:09:09,182 --> 00:09:13,176
Mike Wilson is dead.

113
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,522
They think you're dead.

114
00:09:22,695 --> 00:09:25,096
Your wife's on trial
for murdering you.

115
00:09:25,265 --> 00:09:28,827
Why don't you go down to the
police and straighten this thing out.

116
00:09:29,002 --> 00:09:30,061
I am dead.

117
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,068
Sure, and I'm Robert Redford.

118
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,639
Mr. Matlock, somebody
killed me, but it wasn't my wife.

119
00:09:34,808 --> 00:09:37,277
And I'm not gonna let her
go through life thinking it was.

120
00:09:37,444 --> 00:09:39,310
You need professional help.

121
00:09:39,479 --> 00:09:41,971
Look, I know this is odd
but you've gotta believe me.

122
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:48,013
What are you doing?
Your car's over there.

123
00:09:48,188 --> 00:09:52,421
I know. I'm going across the
street and talk to my friend Pete.

124
00:09:52,959 --> 00:09:56,054
I'm gonna have you arrested.
Maybe they'll commit you.

125
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:01,233
Wait.

126
00:10:02,068 --> 00:10:04,663
I don't know what I
am, okay? Alive. Dead.

127
00:10:04,838 --> 00:10:07,501
It's been a month and I haven't
been able to figure it out myself.

128
00:10:07,674 --> 00:10:10,109
All of sudden, I'm
in contact with you.

129
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:12,802
You're the only one who
can see me or hear me.

130
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:15,138
Hey, Pete.

131
00:10:19,986 --> 00:10:21,978
I guess the only thing
to do is to show you.

132
00:10:32,599 --> 00:10:33,623
Look out!

133
00:10:38,238 --> 00:10:40,036
Get out of the way!

134
00:10:47,447 --> 00:10:48,471
You see?

135
00:10:53,453 --> 00:10:56,116
- Ben?
- Get away from me. Leave me alone.

136
00:10:56,289 --> 00:10:59,589
- Ben?
- Get away from me.

137
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:02,758
Get away. Get away.

138
00:11:03,263 --> 00:11:04,424
Get away.

139
00:11:24,517 --> 00:11:26,748
- Leave me alone. MIKE:
You've gotta help me.

140
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,411
She didn't do it.

141
00:11:28,588 --> 00:11:30,989
Maybe it's something I ate.

142
00:11:31,891 --> 00:11:35,555
There's got to be some
rational explanation.

143
00:11:37,497 --> 00:11:39,932
This can't be happening.

144
00:11:45,805 --> 00:11:47,865
Then why not help me?

145
00:11:48,308 --> 00:11:51,506
I mean, if this is all just a
big dream, what's the harm?

146
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,015
- You are a ghost.
- Of course.

147
00:11:59,152 --> 00:12:00,950
I'm talking to a ghost.

148
00:12:02,722 --> 00:12:03,985
- You're a ghost?
- Yes.

149
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,719
- It's not possible.
- Yes, it is.

150
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:10,062
- I can do more tricks for you.
- No.

151
00:12:16,069 --> 00:12:20,837
What were you and your wife
arguing about that afternoon?

152
00:12:21,307 --> 00:12:23,936
Oh, I don't know. We were
newlyweds. We argued.

153
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:26,375
The only important thing
is that she pushed me

154
00:12:26,546 --> 00:12:29,311
and then she ran out of
the barn. Now, she thinks

155
00:12:29,482 --> 00:12:31,713
that my head hit the
shovel when I fell and I died.

156
00:12:31,884 --> 00:12:34,911
The truth is, someone
came in after she left

157
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:36,886
and used that
shovel to murder me.

158
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:38,482
And you don't know who.

159
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:43,121
I heard a noise, started
to look up, and wham!

160
00:12:43,296 --> 00:12:47,757
The next thing I know, I'm standing
there looking down at a body. Mine.

161
00:12:48,501 --> 00:12:50,231
Oh my.

162
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:52,433
Oh my. I just...

163
00:12:53,706 --> 00:12:55,436
I just don't know.

164
00:12:55,808 --> 00:12:59,142
It wouldn't hurt to
go talk to my wife.

165
00:13:07,754 --> 00:13:08,778
Okay.

166
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:10,990
Yes.

167
00:13:22,869 --> 00:13:24,337
Yes? MATLOCK: Yes.

168
00:13:24,504 --> 00:13:26,439
I'm Ben Matlock, a lawyer.

169
00:13:26,606 --> 00:13:27,699
Isn't she beautiful?

170
00:13:27,874 --> 00:13:31,504
I wonder if I could talk with you
for a minute about your case?

171
00:13:32,679 --> 00:13:34,648
Oh, I already have a lawyer.

172
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:41,482
Well, yes, I know. It's just that,
um, Mike was a kind of friend of mine.

173
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:43,214
Tell her we met
through Uncle Russ

174
00:13:43,356 --> 00:13:45,234
when you did legal work
for him back in Savannah.

175
00:13:45,258 --> 00:13:46,282
I met him in Savannah

176
00:13:46,459 --> 00:13:49,156
while I was doing legal
work for his Uncle Russ.

177
00:13:50,063 --> 00:13:54,797
- Uncle Russ? Heh, what a character.
- Heh, oh, he's a fine man.

178
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:56,207
He passed away last year.

179
00:13:56,302 --> 00:13:58,703
Was a fine man. Was.

180
00:14:00,106 --> 00:14:01,836
Come on in.

181
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:15,615
Have a seat.

182
00:14:16,589 --> 00:14:19,582
- Can I get you something to drink?
- No, thanks.

183
00:14:20,493 --> 00:14:21,859
So?

184
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:23,587
So.

185
00:14:23,996 --> 00:14:28,058
Scott Ainsley's your attorney? I
didn't know he practiced criminal law.

186
00:14:28,568 --> 00:14:30,799
He handled my
husband's business affairs

187
00:14:30,970 --> 00:14:35,772
and my case seemed so
cut-and-dry. I mean, I know I killed Mike.

188
00:14:35,942 --> 00:14:39,936
That's why he pleaded you
innocent by reason of insanity?

189
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:44,979
Scott figured I might only get a
couple of months in an institution.

190
00:14:45,151 --> 00:14:46,676
You think we did
the wrong thing?

191
00:14:46,853 --> 00:14:50,620
I don't know enough
about the case to say.

192
00:14:54,026 --> 00:14:55,517
Um...

193
00:14:55,695 --> 00:15:00,258
That argument, uh, you had with
Mike outside the stable that day,

194
00:15:00,433 --> 00:15:02,800
- what was that about?
- Uh-oh.

195
00:15:02,969 --> 00:15:05,871
Mike had been getting
these anonymous letters

196
00:15:06,038 --> 00:15:07,768
saying that I was
cheating on him.

197
00:15:09,842 --> 00:15:11,402
Well, everything's
under control.

198
00:15:11,544 --> 00:15:15,106
It doesn't look like she's gonna
foal until morning. So, I, uh...

199
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:17,721
- Hi. How are you doing?
- Ben Matlock, this is Keith Garrick.

200
00:15:17,884 --> 00:15:19,409
Keith was Mike's
business partner.

201
00:15:19,585 --> 00:15:20,905
- How are you?
- Nice to meet you.

202
00:15:21,053 --> 00:15:22,398
- How are you?
- He's been incredibly supportive

203
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:23,947
through this whole thing.

204
00:15:24,490 --> 00:15:25,788
Get your hands off her.

205
00:15:25,958 --> 00:15:27,703
Don't know what I
would've done without him.

206
00:15:27,727 --> 00:15:29,025
I hope I'm not interrupting.

207
00:15:29,195 --> 00:15:30,995
- You wanted her all along.
- Go back outside.

208
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:33,395
- Mr. Matlock.
- That's all right. I'll leave.

209
00:15:33,566 --> 00:15:35,330
I wasn't talking to you.

210
00:15:35,501 --> 00:15:37,060
You weren't? MATLOCK: No. No.

211
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:41,367
I mean, well, yes, but I
didn't mean it that way.

212
00:15:41,541 --> 00:15:42,736
You wrote those letters.

213
00:15:42,909 --> 00:15:45,401
You were trying to break
us up so you could have her.

214
00:15:47,914 --> 00:15:49,507
- Are you all right?
- Punch him for me.

215
00:15:49,682 --> 00:15:51,014
No.

216
00:15:51,184 --> 00:15:55,952
I mean, no, I'm not all right.
To tell you the truth, I'd better go.

217
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:58,281
Just one punch. Please, Ben.

218
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:00,282
Just one punch. Come on.

219
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:03,328
Come on. He won't hit you
back. You're older than he is.

220
00:16:03,496 --> 00:16:06,591
I'll be back when he...
When I'm feeling better.

221
00:16:08,334 --> 00:16:10,394
What was that all about?

222
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:13,162
- I have no idea.
- Heh.

223
00:16:13,339 --> 00:16:14,967
Do you wanna get
something to eat?

224
00:16:15,141 --> 00:16:17,235
- Sure.
- Okay.

225
00:16:22,849 --> 00:16:24,147
Oh, Janice.

226
00:16:38,898 --> 00:16:40,127
- So?
- Aah!

227
00:16:40,299 --> 00:16:42,768
Keith is the one who killed
me. I'll bet you anything.

228
00:16:42,935 --> 00:16:44,301
I'm going to bed.

229
00:16:44,470 --> 00:16:46,735
Can't you leave me alone?

230
00:16:47,039 --> 00:16:48,701
You said you'd help
me with the case.

231
00:16:48,875 --> 00:16:50,605
I changed my mind.

232
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:52,906
- Why?
- I'll tell you why.

233
00:16:53,079 --> 00:16:56,743
As insane as it may be, I
accept the fact that you're a ghost.

234
00:16:56,916 --> 00:17:01,513
But you're the most annoying,
ill-mannered ghost I ever heard of.

235
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:04,851
Now, please get out of my room.

236
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,358
<i>Hi.</i>

237
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:40,916
Leave me alone.

238
00:17:41,093 --> 00:17:42,823
<i>Sorry. I can't leave you alone.</i>

239
00:17:42,995 --> 00:17:44,623
- Go away.
<i>- Nope.</i>

240
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:47,699
<i>- I can't.</i>
- I can.

241
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:53,167
Get off my TV!

242
00:17:53,873 --> 00:17:55,000
<i>Can we talk?</i>

243
00:18:01,948 --> 00:18:05,214
You lied to me about the
argument you had with Janice.

244
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:07,777
<i>I was embarrassed.</i>

245
00:18:08,354 --> 00:18:09,583
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

246
00:18:22,401 --> 00:18:24,302
How do you do that?

247
00:18:24,804 --> 00:18:26,363
I don't know.

248
00:18:30,176 --> 00:18:31,474
Here's the deal.

249
00:18:31,644 --> 00:18:35,206
If I'm gonna help, you
have to behave yourself.

250
00:18:35,548 --> 00:18:38,848
And you have to tell me
the truth about Janice.

251
00:18:41,821 --> 00:18:44,021
Like she said, I've been
getting these anonymous letters

252
00:18:44,156 --> 00:18:46,557
saying that she'd been
seeing somebody else.

253
00:18:46,726 --> 00:18:49,958
That's what we were arguing about
that day. I had just gotten another one.

254
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:52,792
- She denied it?
- Yeah.

255
00:18:53,165 --> 00:18:54,565
You didn't believe her?

256
00:18:54,934 --> 00:18:57,927
As you might have noticed, I
have this little jealousy problem.

257
00:18:58,104 --> 00:18:59,504
Yeah.

258
00:19:00,706 --> 00:19:04,336
I figure somewhere along the
line, Keith fell in love with my wife.

259
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:08,838
He sent those letters knowing
how nuts it would make me

260
00:19:09,015 --> 00:19:11,855
and that it was only a matter of
time until Janice left me, as a result.

261
00:19:12,018 --> 00:19:13,042
Yeah.

262
00:19:13,219 --> 00:19:18,180
Only, he got impatient. So
he doubled back that day,

263
00:19:18,357 --> 00:19:19,677
waited for her
to leave the barn,

264
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:23,728
then killed me so that he could
finally have her all to himself.

265
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:36,202
You still have the letters?

266
00:19:38,144 --> 00:19:40,079
They're in my office at home.

267
00:19:42,081 --> 00:19:45,051
If we can trace
them back to Keith,

268
00:19:45,217 --> 00:19:47,277
they might prove
that he's the real killer.

269
00:19:51,123 --> 00:19:53,183
I think I'll have
Conrad look around.

270
00:19:55,828 --> 00:19:57,524
Thanks for helping me, Ben.

271
00:19:58,230 --> 00:19:59,698
It's okay.

272
00:20:00,332 --> 00:20:03,234
- You wanna get off my bed?
- Oh, sure.

273
00:20:07,273 --> 00:20:09,333
How about out of my room?

274
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:10,976
See you in the morning.

275
00:20:34,133 --> 00:20:35,453
You make sure
she's good and dry.

276
00:20:35,601 --> 00:20:37,601
Take her in, give her a
good rubdown, turn her out.

277
00:20:37,770 --> 00:20:39,329
By that time, Speed
Sensation over here

278
00:20:39,505 --> 00:20:41,269
will be ready for
the same treatment.

279
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,635
Gotcha.

280
00:20:42,808 --> 00:20:45,448
You do all that as well as you
handle this horse, you've got a job.

281
00:20:45,945 --> 00:20:47,413
Great.

282
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:50,011
Is Mr. Garrick around?

283
00:20:50,483 --> 00:20:51,576
He's over by the barn.

284
00:20:53,819 --> 00:20:55,481
You know him?

285
00:20:55,955 --> 00:20:58,220
Well, no, I just figured
I'd introduce myself.

286
00:20:58,390 --> 00:21:00,120
I mean, he's one
of the owners, right?

287
00:21:01,494 --> 00:21:03,759
Sucking up to the man
who writes the checks?

288
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,522
It never hurts.

289
00:21:34,794 --> 00:21:37,127
You were supposed to
be here 45 minutes ago.

290
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:39,765
I don't want anyone
to see. Come on.

291
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:45,635
You wanted a few
weeks to think it over,

292
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:47,535
I gave you a few weeks.

293
00:21:49,041 --> 00:21:53,137
Now, what's the answer?
You and your pal in or out?

294
00:21:53,312 --> 00:21:56,942
If anyone found out, you'd
be barred from racing for life.

295
00:21:57,116 --> 00:22:00,712
You own a trotter. It's
odds on to win this Sunday.

296
00:22:00,886 --> 00:22:03,048
Now a man could make
some serious money

297
00:22:03,222 --> 00:22:04,383
knowing she'd lose.

298
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:09,686
Fix it for me and I'll forget
that 200 grand you owe me.

299
00:22:09,862 --> 00:22:11,022
Mr. Petrie, you just can't...

300
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:13,793
I guess that I'm not
making myself clear. Timmy.

301
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:18,570
Make things clear
to Mr. Garrick.

302
00:22:43,395 --> 00:22:44,795
Uh, it's just a horse.

303
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:47,128
Forget it.

304
00:22:50,803 --> 00:22:54,535
I want your answer tomorrow.

305
00:23:10,356 --> 00:23:11,949
Good girl.

306
00:23:34,546 --> 00:23:36,344
What did you find out?

307
00:23:36,782 --> 00:23:39,650
Keith Garrick's got
some serious problems.

308
00:23:39,818 --> 00:23:43,118
- He's into loan sharks for $200,000.
- I knew it was him.

309
00:23:43,289 --> 00:23:45,249
Almost got my head
handed to me out there.

310
00:23:45,391 --> 00:23:46,711
If it wasn't for
a fidgety horse,

311
00:23:46,859 --> 00:23:49,099
some very big guys would've
found me hiding in that barn.

312
00:23:49,395 --> 00:23:50,727
I made the horse sneeze.

313
00:23:50,896 --> 00:23:52,091
Lunch is ready.

314
00:23:54,333 --> 00:23:55,357
Now, listen.

315
00:23:55,534 --> 00:23:57,526
Let's go out to the
farm and nail this sucker.

316
00:23:57,703 --> 00:23:58,966
After I eat.

317
00:23:59,138 --> 00:24:01,058
He's in love with Janice,
up to his neck in debt.

318
00:24:01,206 --> 00:24:04,176
- What more do you need?
- I just... Food, now.

319
00:24:04,777 --> 00:24:06,575
Behave yourself, okay?

320
00:24:23,028 --> 00:24:24,052
Ohh.

321
00:24:24,229 --> 00:24:27,859
Turkey on rye with cranberry
sauce. I could eat five of them.

322
00:24:28,033 --> 00:24:31,128
Conrad, you want a turkey
on rye with cranberry sauce?

323
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:33,329
How did you know?

324
00:24:35,174 --> 00:24:36,335
It was a lucky guess.

325
00:24:38,544 --> 00:24:42,037
Uh, we have to figure out
where Keith Garrick went

326
00:24:42,214 --> 00:24:46,151
when he left Mike Wilson's
farm after the murder.

327
00:24:46,318 --> 00:24:48,583
Does he have an alibi or
could he have doubled back

328
00:24:48,754 --> 00:24:52,418
and gone into the stable
after Janice Wilson left?

329
00:24:52,591 --> 00:24:55,186
You know, Dad, Conrad
and I are just a little confused.

330
00:24:55,361 --> 00:24:57,330
I mean, Janice Wilson
already has an attorney,

331
00:24:57,496 --> 00:25:00,159
and she more or less
admitted to killing her husband.

332
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:05,669
Well, she... She thinks she killed
him, but, uh, somebody else did.

333
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:07,568
Oh. How do you know?

334
00:25:09,708 --> 00:25:11,734
There was a witness.

335
00:25:11,910 --> 00:25:13,503
Oh, yeah?

336
00:25:13,679 --> 00:25:14,977
How come he hasn't come forward?

337
00:25:15,948 --> 00:25:21,319
Well, he's, um, out of
town, kind of permanently.

338
00:25:21,487 --> 00:25:23,649
Are you saying he
refuses to testify?

339
00:25:23,822 --> 00:25:26,121
No, I'm saying he can't.

340
00:25:26,291 --> 00:25:28,487
Leanne, you really
wouldn't understand.

341
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:30,822
Dad, why don't you try me?

342
00:25:36,802 --> 00:25:38,031
Okay.

343
00:25:40,272 --> 00:25:41,672
Uh...

344
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:46,608
I may be a little...
eccentric, but I am rational.

345
00:25:47,513 --> 00:25:48,811
Yeah.

346
00:25:48,981 --> 00:25:53,783
I mean, I don't drink a lot
and no drugs, no hallucination.

347
00:25:53,952 --> 00:25:55,477
Dad, what are you getting at?

348
00:25:56,688 --> 00:26:02,320
Well, the reason I'm getting
involved in the Wilson case is

349
00:26:02,828 --> 00:26:04,456
Mike Wilson wants me to.

350
00:26:05,798 --> 00:26:06,822
Mike Wilson?

351
00:26:07,332 --> 00:26:08,925
The victim?

352
00:26:09,101 --> 00:26:10,364
The dead victim?

353
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:13,795
Yeah.

354
00:26:16,875 --> 00:26:20,368
He's sitting beside
me right now.

355
00:26:25,384 --> 00:26:27,395
You're telling me you
see someone in that chair?

356
00:26:27,419 --> 00:26:28,443
Yeah.

357
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,889
And you talk to him?

358
00:26:31,890 --> 00:26:33,256
Yeah.

359
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:36,293
Oh, and that's why
we're on the case?

360
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:38,093
- Yeah.
- Heh.

361
00:26:39,098 --> 00:26:42,000
You know, Dad, you haven't
been sleeping well lately.

362
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:43,863
- Yeah. LEANNE:
You just mentioned that

363
00:26:44,036 --> 00:26:45,265
the other day.

364
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:47,303
So I tell you what you're
gonna do. Just relax,

365
00:26:47,473 --> 00:26:49,169
take a couple of days off.

366
00:26:49,575 --> 00:26:51,976
Conrad and I are on it now.

367
00:27:01,019 --> 00:27:02,180
No.

368
00:27:06,058 --> 00:27:08,584
I'll handle it myself.

369
00:27:09,495 --> 00:27:11,020
Dad?

370
00:27:12,164 --> 00:27:13,188
Dad?

371
00:27:17,536 --> 00:27:21,732
Do you think my
father is... Nuts?

372
00:27:34,553 --> 00:27:37,751
I sure am glad I told Conrad
and Leanne about you.

373
00:27:37,923 --> 00:27:40,119
Hmm, sorry that didn't work out.

374
00:27:40,292 --> 00:27:42,659
They think I'm crazy.

375
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,423
Who's that?

376
00:27:46,598 --> 00:27:49,033
Stuart Cokely, our trainer.

377
00:27:49,201 --> 00:27:51,466
The man's been working
on that trailer for months.

378
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:53,162
Stay here.

379
00:27:54,940 --> 00:27:56,067
I mean it.

380
00:27:56,241 --> 00:27:59,268
Go on back there
or I'm going home.

381
00:28:01,413 --> 00:28:02,847
Okay.

382
00:28:11,056 --> 00:28:12,080
- Hi.
- Hi.

383
00:28:12,257 --> 00:28:13,782
- Can I help you?
- Yeah.

384
00:28:13,959 --> 00:28:17,726
I'm Ben Matlock, lawyer. I'm
kind of helping out on the case.

385
00:28:17,896 --> 00:28:19,023
Is Janice home?

386
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:22,134
Uh, left about a half hour
ago. Had to be in court.

387
00:28:22,301 --> 00:28:23,428
Doggone.

388
00:28:23,602 --> 00:28:26,128
She said she was gonna leave
something for me in the house.

389
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:27,637
Do you suppose it's open?

390
00:28:27,806 --> 00:28:30,776
- You can try it.
- Yeah. Yeah.

391
00:28:31,944 --> 00:28:35,142
Well, that was a terrible thing
that happened to Mike, wasn't it?

392
00:28:36,114 --> 00:28:37,309
Yeah.

393
00:28:37,482 --> 00:28:38,848
Yeah.

394
00:28:39,484 --> 00:28:40,577
Were you here that day?

395
00:28:40,752 --> 00:28:44,519
Yeah. I was turning out some
horses and I heard Mrs. Wilson scream.

396
00:28:44,690 --> 00:28:46,682
And like you said, it
was a terrible thing.

397
00:28:46,858 --> 00:28:48,121
I'll say it was.

398
00:28:48,293 --> 00:28:50,888
I understand that Keith
Garrick was here that afternoon.

399
00:28:51,063 --> 00:28:52,531
Yeah. He'd just left.

400
00:28:53,465 --> 00:28:56,264
So he wasn't one of them that
came running into the stable

401
00:28:56,435 --> 00:28:58,131
after Janice found the body?

402
00:28:58,303 --> 00:29:00,067
Nope. Long gone.

403
00:29:03,275 --> 00:29:06,302
- Thanks for your time, heh.
- It's okay.

404
00:29:17,623 --> 00:29:21,025
I kept the letters locked
up in the desk drawer.

405
00:29:22,527 --> 00:29:24,325
The key's gone.

406
00:29:24,496 --> 00:29:26,556
You'll just have to break in.

407
00:29:31,903 --> 00:29:32,927
They're gone.

408
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:35,645
Did Janice know where
you kept the letters?

409
00:29:35,807 --> 00:29:37,708
She didn't know I kept
them at all. Nobody did.

410
00:29:37,876 --> 00:29:40,539
- Not even Keith?
- Not even Keith.

411
00:29:42,814 --> 00:29:44,614
Who knew where you
kept the key to the drawer?

412
00:29:47,152 --> 00:29:48,950
Good question.

413
00:29:49,121 --> 00:29:50,350
You wanna go downtown?

414
00:29:50,522 --> 00:29:52,218
- It's not Keith?
- It's Keith.

415
00:29:52,391 --> 00:29:54,360
I think I know how to prove it.

416
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:09,605
It was Scott Ainsley. He's the only
one who knew where I kept that key.

417
00:30:09,775 --> 00:30:11,895
As Janice's lawyer, I'm
sure she let him in the office

418
00:30:12,044 --> 00:30:14,479
- to go through my papers.
- Well, if he's your lawyer,

419
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:16,774
I guess he and Keith could
have been up to something.

420
00:30:16,948 --> 00:30:18,678
- Uh-huh.
- Um...

421
00:30:18,850 --> 00:30:21,649
- Go on.
- I'd be breaking and entering.

422
00:30:22,187 --> 00:30:23,519
You're not breaking anything.

423
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:26,850
Well, I guess I'm
just trespassing.

424
00:30:27,025 --> 00:30:29,153
And in the company of a ghost.

425
00:30:32,798 --> 00:30:36,132
If he did steal those letters,
he probably threw them away

426
00:30:36,301 --> 00:30:41,706
a long time ago and why
would he steal them for Keith?

427
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:45,074
- Now what?
- Over there.

428
00:30:45,243 --> 00:30:48,338
Open that. The ledger
for the farm is in there.

429
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:52,317
Scott Ainsley was an accountant?

430
00:30:52,484 --> 00:30:54,817
No, we just kept all
the papers in his office.

431
00:30:54,986 --> 00:30:57,182
Open it to the last entry.

432
00:30:57,656 --> 00:31:01,218
I died before I got a chance to
review the figures for the last quarter.

433
00:31:01,393 --> 00:31:04,363
You think Scott Ainsley
was doctoring the books?

434
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,555
I know he was.

435
00:31:11,103 --> 00:31:13,595
Ben Matlock? What are you doing?

436
00:31:13,772 --> 00:31:19,473
I was just, uh, going over the
ledger for the, uh, Wilson horse farm.

437
00:31:20,512 --> 00:31:24,916
Hi, Mr. Garrick. Do you two
fellows always meet this late at night?

438
00:31:25,717 --> 00:31:26,776
I'm calling the police.

439
00:31:26,952 --> 00:31:30,116
Do that and I'm sure they'd
be as fascinated as I am.

440
00:31:30,288 --> 00:31:31,415
What are you talking about?

441
00:31:32,157 --> 00:31:34,456
Well, for one thing...

442
00:31:36,428 --> 00:31:37,805
Keith's been
embezzling from the farm

443
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:39,957
and Scott Ainsley's
been helping him.

444
00:31:40,332 --> 00:31:44,030
According to the ledger, uh, Keith
here has been skimming funds,

445
00:31:44,202 --> 00:31:47,434
probably to pay off loan sharks.

446
00:31:47,606 --> 00:31:51,668
And you've been helping
him, for a small fee, no doubt.

447
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:54,876
My accountant, Dennis Prescott,
should be able to confirm it.

448
00:31:55,046 --> 00:31:57,277
I'm sure that Dennis
Prescott could confirm

449
00:31:57,449 --> 00:31:59,509
that these figures
have been altered.

450
00:32:01,319 --> 00:32:03,479
He sent those letters because
he's in love with Janice.

451
00:32:05,490 --> 00:32:06,514
Excuse me?

452
00:32:06,691 --> 00:32:10,958
I'm saying that the two of you
have been cooking the books,

453
00:32:11,129 --> 00:32:13,621
and successfully,
till times got tough.

454
00:32:13,799 --> 00:32:17,099
And then, uh, when Mike
got worried about money,

455
00:32:17,269 --> 00:32:20,535
you figured you'd better
do something to distract him

456
00:32:20,705 --> 00:32:23,402
and so you sent
him those letters.

457
00:32:23,575 --> 00:32:28,445
And then one or both of you
got afraid that that wasn't enough

458
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:31,208
and so you killed him.

459
00:32:31,383 --> 00:32:33,045
Now how could you
possibly know that?

460
00:32:33,218 --> 00:32:35,744
What the hell difference does it
make how he knows? He knows.

461
00:32:35,921 --> 00:32:38,117
Uh, you could
kill me too, but...

462
00:32:40,392 --> 00:32:44,420
We may have sent those letters,
Mr. Matlock, but we didn't kill Mike.

463
00:32:44,596 --> 00:32:46,121
As it happens, we have an alibi.

464
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:47,891
- Shut up.
- No.

465
00:32:48,533 --> 00:32:50,365
If he tells,

466
00:32:51,503 --> 00:32:53,335
it is over.

467
00:32:53,505 --> 00:32:56,475
Look, it's not exactly a
brilliant career move for me.

468
00:32:56,641 --> 00:32:59,167
We don't have a choice.

469
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:02,804
At the time of the murder?

470
00:33:02,981 --> 00:33:05,974
We were meeting with a
man named Ross Petrie.

471
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:07,346
He's a local loan shark.

472
00:33:08,353 --> 00:33:11,949
You can ask him or anybody
at that social club he owns.

473
00:33:12,624 --> 00:33:14,217
That's where we met.

474
00:33:16,461 --> 00:33:17,827
You were both there?

475
00:33:19,264 --> 00:33:21,392
God help us, yes.

476
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,756
This has got to work. - Yeah?

477
00:33:46,558 --> 00:33:48,836
You've got to talk Janice
into using you as her lawyer.

478
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:52,228
I'll do the best I
can. Stay here.

479
00:33:52,397 --> 00:33:54,025
Forget it.

480
00:34:04,309 --> 00:34:06,073
- Mr. Matlock.
- Hi, Ms. Wilson.

481
00:34:06,244 --> 00:34:09,737
I called Aunt Mel, Uncle
Russ' widow in Savannah.

482
00:34:09,915 --> 00:34:11,645
She's never heard
of you, Mr. Matlock.

483
00:34:11,816 --> 00:34:13,682
She said if you did legal
work for Uncle Russ,

484
00:34:13,852 --> 00:34:14,876
she'd know who you were.

485
00:34:15,921 --> 00:34:19,016
Uh, she's right, Ms. Wilson.

486
00:34:19,190 --> 00:34:20,385
I did lie to you.

487
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:23,256
I never did any legal
work for your Uncle Russ

488
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:26,887
and I didn't know your
husband 10 years ago.

489
00:34:28,133 --> 00:34:31,331
Why? Why did you lie?

490
00:34:31,503 --> 00:34:32,527
Why are you here?

491
00:34:32,704 --> 00:34:35,833
Have you ever believed
something was wrong and known

492
00:34:36,007 --> 00:34:40,308
- you had to do something about it?
- It doesn't explain why you lied.

493
00:34:41,146 --> 00:34:44,742
Uh, I wanted to talk
with you, Ms. Wilson.

494
00:34:44,916 --> 00:34:46,248
I might be able to help.

495
00:34:46,418 --> 00:34:48,910
I know that Scott Ainsley
resigned your case this morning

496
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:52,319
and I thought maybe you
would let me represent you.

497
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:56,560
Why do you wanna be
involved in my case so badly?

498
00:34:58,597 --> 00:34:59,690
Tell her the truth.

499
00:35:00,198 --> 00:35:02,861
I believe that you're innocent.

500
00:35:03,034 --> 00:35:05,560
And if... If what
I believe is true,

501
00:35:05,737 --> 00:35:10,766
then you shouldn't... You shouldn't
go to jail for something you didn't do.

502
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:16,775
So, Mrs. Wilson, what
have you got to lose?

503
00:35:20,151 --> 00:35:21,619
Come on, Janice.

504
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:25,215
I think you're crazy.

505
00:35:25,557 --> 00:35:27,423
But you are right
about one thing.

506
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:29,559
I have nothing to lose.

507
00:35:38,570 --> 00:35:39,594
Yes!

508
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:43,875
All right. You did it.

509
00:35:45,276 --> 00:35:47,074
Wanna get to work?

510
00:35:48,346 --> 00:35:51,805
- I'm gonna kill you.
- It's too late.

511
00:36:01,292 --> 00:36:04,091
I say Scott and Keith are lying
about being with Ross Petrie.

512
00:36:04,262 --> 00:36:06,060
Come on, Mike.

513
00:36:06,231 --> 00:36:09,690
If they were lying, they would have
said they were with a priest or a rabbi

514
00:36:09,868 --> 00:36:13,737
or Queen of England,
not some Mob person.

515
00:36:13,905 --> 00:36:15,635
Well, who killed me?

516
00:36:16,207 --> 00:36:18,904
Uh, somebody from
your past, maybe.

517
00:36:19,077 --> 00:36:21,171
I was a nice guy,
Ben. People like me.

518
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:25,914
Well, there was Mel
Whitaker over in Macon.

519
00:36:26,084 --> 00:36:29,577
He didn't like me a whole
lot. Sold me a bum horse.

520
00:36:29,754 --> 00:36:31,434
There was Harold
Ramsey up in Branderville,

521
00:36:31,589 --> 00:36:33,114
thought I'd sold
him a bum horse.

522
00:36:35,427 --> 00:36:38,022
Branderville? Why does
that sound so familiar?

523
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:44,335
- What is that smell? MIKE:
Probably horse liniment.

524
00:36:44,502 --> 00:36:46,869
Hmm. Horse liniment?

525
00:36:47,906 --> 00:36:49,636
You know what?

526
00:36:50,442 --> 00:36:53,571
That's what I smelled
in here just before I died.

527
00:36:53,978 --> 00:36:55,002
Horse liniment?

528
00:36:56,881 --> 00:37:00,181
Ben, somebody's watching.

529
00:37:02,187 --> 00:37:03,712
Oh, Mr. Cokely.

530
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:09,221
Ms. Wilson said that I
could look around in here.

531
00:37:09,394 --> 00:37:11,795
Hey, it's fine by me.

532
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:14,665
Ben,

533
00:37:15,133 --> 00:37:16,601
something's wrong.

534
00:37:17,969 --> 00:37:19,631
Something's wrong.

535
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:26,571
His riding boots.

536
00:37:26,745 --> 00:37:28,873
He's not wearing riding boots.

537
00:37:29,047 --> 00:37:30,811
That's what's wrong.

538
00:37:37,021 --> 00:37:39,616
Benjamin Matlock for
the defense, Your Honor.

539
00:37:39,791 --> 00:37:43,523
At the defendant's request,
I have replaced Mr. Ainsley.

540
00:37:43,695 --> 00:37:46,995
Very well. If you're ready to
proceed, by all means, go ahead.

541
00:37:47,165 --> 00:37:51,364
Yes, sir. Defense calls
Stuart Cokely to the stand.

542
00:38:01,012 --> 00:38:02,640
You're toast, pal.

543
00:38:02,814 --> 00:38:04,715
Where are you from?

544
00:38:04,883 --> 00:38:06,545
Branderville, Kentucky.

545
00:38:06,718 --> 00:38:11,213
That's right. That's right. I saw that
name on your license plate frame

546
00:38:11,389 --> 00:38:14,325
on the back of your
horse trailer. Yeah.

547
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:16,927
Uh, is the name, uh...

548
00:38:17,095 --> 00:38:19,326
Does the name Harold
Ramsey mean anything to you?

549
00:38:21,032 --> 00:38:22,660
That's my stepfather's name.

550
00:38:24,035 --> 00:38:26,834
- Is he deceased?
- Yes.

551
00:38:27,872 --> 00:38:28,896
How did he die?

552
00:38:29,941 --> 00:38:32,877
He committed suicide
about four years ago.

553
00:38:34,279 --> 00:38:36,680
You loved your stepfather
very much, didn't you?

554
00:38:38,249 --> 00:38:41,310
Loved him a lot more than I
loved my real father, that's for sure.

555
00:38:41,486 --> 00:38:43,421
What did he do for a living?

556
00:38:43,588 --> 00:38:45,750
Raised racehorses.
Taught me everything I know.

557
00:38:45,924 --> 00:38:47,364
Three months before he died,

558
00:38:47,525 --> 00:38:52,429
he purchased a champion racehorse
by the name of Workmen's Way.

559
00:38:52,597 --> 00:38:57,058
Planned to put him out to stud.
Paid a million dollars for him.

560
00:38:57,235 --> 00:38:58,915
- Is that right? STUART:
Yes, that's right.

561
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:01,630
Well, what happened
to Workmen's Way?

562
00:39:02,006 --> 00:39:05,238
Well, about two weeks
after we got him, he died.

563
00:39:05,410 --> 00:39:08,278
Turns out he had
some rare disease.

564
00:39:08,980 --> 00:39:10,471
Any insurance?

565
00:39:10,648 --> 00:39:14,346
No. My father... My stepfather
hadn't quite gotten around to that yet.

566
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:19,716
So when that horse died,
your stepfather lost everything.

567
00:39:19,891 --> 00:39:24,352
His horses, his farm,
his savings, everything.

568
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:25,758
- Didn't he?
- Yes.

569
00:39:25,930 --> 00:39:30,664
Within three months, he was
penniless and that's why he killed himself.

570
00:39:31,469 --> 00:39:32,994
Yeah.

571
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:39,070
Who sold that horse
to your stepfather?

572
00:39:41,980 --> 00:39:43,881
Mike Wilson.

573
00:39:44,983 --> 00:39:47,179
And your stepfather,
Harold Ramsey,

574
00:39:47,552 --> 00:39:52,047
was convinced that Mike Wilson
knew that that horse was sick

575
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:54,317
- when he sold it to you.
- Yes.

576
00:39:54,492 --> 00:39:56,427
Then, when in despair
he killed himself,

577
00:39:56,594 --> 00:40:01,294
you in turn blamed Mike
Wilson for his death, didn't you?

578
00:40:01,466 --> 00:40:03,492
- No.
- Oh, come on, Stuart.

579
00:40:06,604 --> 00:40:11,167
Out of all the horse
farms in the country,

580
00:40:11,342 --> 00:40:15,006
you chose Mike
Wilson's to go to work at.

581
00:40:15,179 --> 00:40:18,911
Is that just a coincidence or did
you choose to go to work there

582
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:24,215
so you could wait for your opportunity
to avenge your stepfather's death?

583
00:40:24,389 --> 00:40:25,948
Of course not.

584
00:40:27,158 --> 00:40:30,492
Let me just say, uh, with
your permission, Your Honor,

585
00:40:31,529 --> 00:40:34,590
I have it on good authority
that Mike Wilson did not know

586
00:40:34,766 --> 00:40:39,602
that horse was sick when
he sold him to your stepfather.

587
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:43,469
He was very saddened to
learn of Mr. Ramsey's death.

588
00:40:43,641 --> 00:40:48,272
But anyway, uh, this
picture appeared in the paper

589
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:52,383
a few days before
Mike was killed.

590
00:40:52,917 --> 00:40:56,285
That's Mike. That's Janice.
That's you, isn't it, Mr. Cokely.

591
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:57,786
Yeah, that's me.

592
00:40:57,956 --> 00:41:01,552
Those riding boots are kind
of your trademark, aren't they?

593
00:41:01,726 --> 00:41:03,194
They belonged to my stepfather.

594
00:41:03,361 --> 00:41:06,126
No wonder you wear
them all the time.

595
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:07,321
Or at least you did.

596
00:41:07,498 --> 00:41:10,832
A couple of your coworkers out
at the farm are prepared to testify

597
00:41:11,002 --> 00:41:15,997
that you haven't worn these boots
since the day Mike Wilson was killed.

598
00:41:16,174 --> 00:41:17,198
Why is that?

599
00:41:19,210 --> 00:41:20,735
Just didn't feel like it.

600
00:41:21,112 --> 00:41:22,307
Liar.

601
00:41:23,748 --> 00:41:28,243
These are, uh, the
shoes Mike was wearing

602
00:41:29,387 --> 00:41:32,846
when he was killed. See, there's
a stain up here in the toe area.

603
00:41:33,024 --> 00:41:34,686
See that there?

604
00:41:34,959 --> 00:41:37,155
And these are

605
00:41:38,696 --> 00:41:43,657
the boots Janice was wearing
when she allegedly caused his death.

606
00:41:43,835 --> 00:41:45,861
See? They're stained too.

607
00:41:47,238 --> 00:41:52,939
And these, ugh, are your
boots, aren't they, Mr. Cokely?

608
00:41:53,111 --> 00:41:55,637
The police removed it from
your apartment an hour ago,

609
00:41:55,813 --> 00:41:58,282
with a warrant. But look here,

610
00:41:58,449 --> 00:42:01,214
stain on the toe
of the boot. See?

611
00:42:03,254 --> 00:42:06,713
Stain on the toe
of this boot, too.

612
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:09,793
Why is that?

613
00:42:12,797 --> 00:42:14,857
I think I know.

614
00:42:15,166 --> 00:42:16,828
There was a bottle
of horse liniment

615
00:42:17,001 --> 00:42:18,867
that got knocked over
during the argument

616
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:21,939
between Mike and
Janice that day.

617
00:42:22,106 --> 00:42:24,871
It's right here, isn't
it? In the police report.

618
00:42:25,043 --> 00:42:26,944
It says that...

619
00:42:27,345 --> 00:42:32,306
Says it had spilled all over the
straw on the floor next to Mike's body.

620
00:42:32,483 --> 00:42:36,181
That means anybody walking
through that straw would have gotten

621
00:42:36,487 --> 00:42:38,319
a stain on their boots.

622
00:42:38,489 --> 00:42:40,981
And that's what this stain is,

623
00:42:41,159 --> 00:42:42,388
horse liniment.

624
00:42:44,095 --> 00:42:47,429
Strong. So strong, you
can still smell it. Mm.

625
00:42:47,598 --> 00:42:49,863
Smells kind of like aftershave.

626
00:42:53,137 --> 00:42:55,629
These boots meant
a great deal to you.

627
00:42:55,807 --> 00:42:58,936
That's why you kept them
instead of throwing them away.

628
00:42:59,110 --> 00:43:01,875
But you never wore
them again after that day

629
00:43:02,046 --> 00:43:03,571
because you knew
that they proved

630
00:43:04,148 --> 00:43:09,553
that after Janice ran out of
that barn, you went in there

631
00:43:10,288 --> 00:43:13,656
and hit Mike Wilson over
the head with that shovel.

632
00:43:14,992 --> 00:43:17,223
That's how you got these stains.

633
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:20,064
You killed Mike Wilson,

634
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:22,423
didn't you, Mr. Cokely?

635
00:43:26,704 --> 00:43:29,970
I'd just as soon not answer
that until I talk to my lawyer.

636
00:43:30,141 --> 00:43:31,769
Yes!

637
00:43:32,477 --> 00:43:35,447
Your Honor, the prosecution
moves that the charges

638
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:37,844
against the defendant
be dismissed.

639
00:43:38,015 --> 00:43:41,383
So moved. Case dismissed.
Court is adjourned.

640
00:44:11,048 --> 00:44:12,448
Well,

641
00:44:13,184 --> 00:44:14,743
mission accomplished.

642
00:44:21,259 --> 00:44:22,784
Yeah.

643
00:44:23,528 --> 00:44:24,860
I guess so.

644
00:44:25,796 --> 00:44:28,493
See that Janice is
okay, would you?

645
00:44:29,367 --> 00:44:32,201
Tell her I'm sorry
I was jealous.

646
00:44:32,904 --> 00:44:35,965
I really wanted her
to be happy with me.

647
00:44:37,542 --> 00:44:39,670
And now I just want
her to be happy.

648
00:44:41,112 --> 00:44:42,637
I will.

649
00:44:47,451 --> 00:44:49,147
Goodbye, Ben.

650
00:44:50,488 --> 00:44:52,116
Thanks.

651
00:45:05,903 --> 00:45:07,963
Will Mr. Wilson be
joining us for lunch today

652
00:45:08,139 --> 00:45:10,165
or does he have other plans?

653
00:45:10,341 --> 00:45:14,176
Uh, no. No. Mike's gone.

654
00:45:14,345 --> 00:45:15,813
- He is?
- Mm-hm.

655
00:45:15,980 --> 00:45:20,975
Yeah. Apparently, he was allowed
to hang around for awhile after he died

656
00:45:21,152 --> 00:45:22,984
to straighten
things up for his wife

657
00:45:23,154 --> 00:45:25,589
and after he'd done
that, his reprise was over.

658
00:45:27,458 --> 00:45:31,862
Dad, I talked to a couple of people
and here's what they think happened.

659
00:45:32,029 --> 00:45:35,158
You read about Mike's
death in the paper,

660
00:45:35,333 --> 00:45:37,325
and something about
it piqued your interest

661
00:45:37,501 --> 00:45:40,562
in a totally subconscious way.

662
00:45:40,738 --> 00:45:44,072
Leanne, I had never heard
of Mike Wilson before this.

663
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:45,266
You read about him.

664
00:45:45,443 --> 00:45:47,469
You saw a picture of
him and Stuart Cokely,

665
00:45:47,645 --> 00:45:50,581
and your subconscious
mind repressed it

666
00:45:50,748 --> 00:45:53,912
and invented this ghost
thing as a way of legitimizing

667
00:45:54,085 --> 00:45:55,644
you getting
involved in the case.

668
00:45:55,820 --> 00:45:58,654
My mind is not
playing tricks on me.

669
00:45:58,990 --> 00:46:02,017
The subconscious
is very powerful.

670
00:46:02,193 --> 00:46:06,255
It's the only thing that makes
any sense and you know it.

671
00:46:13,004 --> 00:46:14,097
You could be right,

672
00:46:20,578 --> 00:46:22,410
but you're not.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
